@*
    The @inherits directive is used to specify the base class that the Razor view inherits from. In this case, it is inheriting from the "Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Razor.RazorPage<TModel>" class, 
    where TModel is a generic type parameter representing the model type for the view. This allows the view to have access to the properties and methods of the specified base class, 
    enabling it to work with strongly typed models and perform various operations related to rendering HTML content.
*@
<!DOCTYPE html>

<html>
<head>
    @*The meta charset tag specifies the character encoding for the HTML document. 
      UTF-8 is a widely used character encoding that can represent almost all characters in the Unicode standard. It is recommended to use UTF-8 for 
      web pages to ensure proper rendering of text, especially for internationalization and multilingual content.
    *@
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    @* The ViewBag.Title property is simply a string object. In this case it's being used in the view to actually define the Title property. *@
    <title>@ViewBag.Title</title>
    @*
        The importmap script tag is used to define an import map for JavaScript modules. Import maps allow you to control the behavior of module imports in the browser, 
        enabling you to specify how module specifiers are resolved to actual URLs. This can be useful for managing dependencies and organizing your JavaScript code.
    *@
    <script type="importmap"></script>    
    @*
        Looking to quickly add Bootstrap to your project
        The link tags are used to include external CSS stylesheets in the HTML document. In this case, the first link tag includes the Bootstrap CSS framework, 
        which provides a set of pre-designed styles and components for building responsive and visually appealing web pages. The second link tag includes a custom CSS file named "account.css" 
        that can be used to define additional styles specific to the account-related pages of the application.
    *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="~/lib/bootstrap/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css" />
    @*
        The link tags are used to include external CSS stylesheets in the HTML document. In this case, the first link tag includes the Bootstrap CSS framework, 
        which provides a set of pre-designed styles and components for building responsive and visually appealing web pages. The second link tag includes a custom CSS file named "account.css" 
        that can be used to define additional styles specific to the account-related pages of the application.
    *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="~/css/account.css" />
</head>
<body>
    <div>
        @* 
            The @RenderBody() method is used in a layout page to render the content of the view that is using that layout. 
            It acts as a placeholder where the content of the specific view will be injected when the page is rendered. 
            This allows for a consistent layout across multiple views while still allowing each view to provide its own unique content.
        *@
        @RenderBody()
    </div>

  @*
        The script tags are used to include external JavaScript files in the HTML document. In this case, the first script tag includes the jQuery library, 
        which is a popular JavaScript library that simplifies DOM manipulation and event handling. The second script tag includes the Bootstrap JavaScript bundle, 
        which provides additional functionality for Bootstrap components such as modals, dropdowns, and carousels. The third script tag includes a custom JavaScript file named "site.js" 
        that can be used to define additional scripts specific to the application. The asp-append-version="true" attribute is used to append a version query string to the URL of the script file, 
        which helps with cache busting and ensures that the browser loads the latest version of the script when it changes.
  *@
    <script src="~/lib/jquery/dist/jquery.min.js"></script>
    <script src="~/lib/bootstrap/dist/js/bootstrap.bundle.min.js"></script>
    <script src="~/js/site.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
    @*
        The @RenderSectionAsync("Scripts", required: false) method is used in a layout page to render a specific section of content defined in the view that is using that layout. 
        In this case, it is looking for a section named "Scripts". The required: false parameter indicates that this section is optional, meaning that if the view does not define a "Scripts" section, 
        the layout will still render without any errors. This allows for flexibility in including additional scripts on specific pages while maintaining a consistent layout.
    *@
    @await RenderSectionAsync("Scripts", required: false)
</body>
</html>
